This file exists only to keep Content/Maps/ in Git — Git tracks files, not
directories, and an empty directory would vanish on clone.

Arena.umap is NOT committed by default: it is generated on demand with

    Scripts/generate-map.sh

which creates a deliberately empty level. The whole arena (floor, walls,
endzones, lights, player starts) is built in C++ by ATraceArenaBuilder at
BeginPlay, so the map asset carries no content and nothing in the game depends
on a .uasset we author.

If the team ever does commit Arena.umap, it goes through Git LFS and is
`lockable` (see .gitattributes) — .umap files cannot be merged, so lock before
you edit:

    git lfs lock Content/Maps/Arena.umap
